Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:58:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Setup 0.9.1: Python 3.10 without uv's minor-version junction
 (fixes Windows error 448)

On some PCs (e.g. OneDrive Files On-Demand or security software) Windows
blocks the 'cpython-3.10-windows-x86_64-none' junction that uv 0.13 always
makes after unpacking Python ("untrusted mount point", os error 448), and
0.9.0 stopped with a wrong "internet connection?" hint.

- Python 3.10.22 is pinned and requested with 'uv python install 3.10.22
  --no-bin --no-registry'; a failure after unpacking is accepted, because
  only the real cpython-3.10.22-... folder is used
- the venv is made with 'uv venv --python <full path to python.exe>' and
  UV_PYTHON_INSTALL_DIR unset, so it never points through the junction;
  pyvenv.cfg 'home' is checked and corrected if it does
- fallbacks: the same python-build-standalone archive downloaded directly
  (SHA-256 pinned, unpacked with Windows' tar.exe), then an installed
  64-bit Python 3.10 (py -3.10-64, PATH, the usual python.org folders)
- a Python already unpacked by a failed run is reused and a half-made venv
  is replaced, so the repair resumes
- UV_PYTHON_DOWNLOADS=manual: uv never fetches a Python by itself
- errors show uv's own message; error 448 gets an accurate hint
- tests/test_setup_runtime_ps1.py: runs the script under pwsh with fake
  uv / python / nvidia-smi, incl. the 448 failure and every fallback
- version 0.9.1; INSTALL_WINDOWS.txt troubleshooting note
